WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:00.667
John.

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:03.670
We do have some police scanner audio.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.272
So this is right before we're told that

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.576
the police beat Tyre Nichols.

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:10.143
So this is

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.811
then when I think they're first

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:12.579
pulling him over.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.381
So let's listen to that.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.784
We got one more black runs

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:18.785
from

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.354
this vehicle from overseas, right?

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.556
A relative of one running on the run,

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.827
it running as a twin as well.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.262
So we don't care

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.064
if he's fighting a decent

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.499
object for that.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.434
What do you hear there, John?

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.669
So I hear they've made the stop,

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.138
but we don't hear that part.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.773
And then he's running

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.341
and then he comes on and says, run

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.610
that tag and see where it comes back to.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.512
So he's gotten away

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.546
and they're trying to figure out,

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.514
well, if he's running home,

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:48.281
where is that?

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.516
Because it could be nearby.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.350
And of course it is.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.584
It's about half mile away.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.286
And that's standard police stuff, right?

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:53.853
That's right.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:54.421
I mean, that's

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.090
that's that's what they should be doing.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.426
And then the next person you hear on

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.327
the air has caught up to him

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:04.531
and is fighting and calls out the street

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:06.900
that it's happening on, which is history.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.102
He's about 80 yards from his home

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.337
and then he's calling for backup.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:15.375
So there's a whole bunch of questions

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.743
that Shimon says,

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.911
you know, still need to be answered.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.613
But let's go through a couple of them.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.215
What was the stop for?

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.149
This is a missing piece.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.051
They said reckless driving originally.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.920
But what was the reckless driving?

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.321
No one's articulated that.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:30.924
What was the first

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.292
altercation about that

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:33.093
resulted in him

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.929
being pepper sprayed and running away?

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.564
And then what was the second

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.232
altercation about?

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.934
All of these are still blanks.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.836
And what we've been told

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:44.471
is that when the tape is released,

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:45.505
you're going to see the incident

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:46.806
from end to end

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:47.407
and some,

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.475
if not all, of these questions

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.375
will be answered.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:49.809
Shimon,

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:50.343
one of the things

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.344
that the police were charged with

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.879
was aggravated kidnaping,

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.013
and that got people's attention

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.381
because what does that mean?

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.182
So, you know,

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.851
I know that you asked that question.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:02:00.453
We were told that that meant that he was

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.822
sort of unlawfully detained

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.524
or contained somehow.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:07.594
Do you have any more information on that?

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:10.096
Yeah, that was one of those charges

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:10.730
that really,

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.066
I think, caught many of us by surprise

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.701
because you certainly never see this

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.137
in these kinds of cases.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:18.238
So we don't have any clarity.

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:18.938
The way the D.A.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:19.772
explained it is

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:23.776
you may have had an initial proper stop

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.545
and they may or may have

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.413
that may have been legal, let's say.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.982
And then as you go through the

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:30.150
through this encounter

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:30.550
and then you go

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.118
into the second encounter,

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.720
then that is where

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.854
that may have occurred,

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:36.556
where was an illegal detainment

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:37.790
of some kind.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.926
And because of the nature of this

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.227
and how this all unfolded,

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.263
and their aggravating circumstances,

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.331
that's why they charged this kidnap.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:46.399
Remember, there are also

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.602
the allegations here

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:50.136
that the

00:02:50.136 --> 00:02:50.603
victim here

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.437
was handcuffed

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.605
during this time

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.607
during some of this beating.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:55.441
Certainly, the D.A.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.509
wouldn't talk about that.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.277
And that is something

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:59.245
we will likely see in the video.

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.848
So that could pertain to that as well.

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:03.750
John, they're going to release

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.250
this video,

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.452
we're told, tomorrow night at 6 p.m..

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:09.889
That's a Friday night at 6 p.m..

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:12.392
Does that make sense to you? Does that.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.861
Is that sort of ripe for trouble?

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:18.097
If this were in New York City

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.000
and I was in the NYPD, and this came up,

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:24.137
I would want this on a Tuesday,

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.206
a school night. A work night. Yeah.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.576
But I think what you're seeing

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:32.078
in Memphis is

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.580
they have delivered

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.281
the beginning of justice.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.783
They have brought extraordinarily

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.817
serious charges

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.420
and a slew of them against each officer.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.522
They have arrested them.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.691
And, you know, one of them has made bail.

00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:46.693
Others are trying to raise bond,

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.194
but they are now in the system.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:49.195
And I think

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:51.531
the way they are choreographing this is

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.833
let's make sure that people see

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.501
that justice is being done.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.703
That's the beginning of it.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.204
And then we'll release the tape,

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.273
because if they did them together,

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.075
I think justice would have been largely

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:04.344
drowned out by the shock over the tape.

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:05.378
I think they wanted people

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:06.212
to digest that.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.481
The that the system is working

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.616
and then see the tape.

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:12.652
And then they have all day today.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:13.720
They have tonight

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.154
and they have all day tomorrow up

00:04:15.154 --> 00:04:16.623
until 5:00

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.391
when they're going to release six

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.659
I should clarify, 6 p.m.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:21.361
local time in Memphis, 7 p.m.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:21.961
7 p.m.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:25.665
here to do that community outreach to say

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:26.666
if we're going to march,

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:27.700
let's march together.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.668
If we're going to protest,

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:29.869
let's protest peacefully.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:31.204
And I

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:33.206
think that Memphis

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:34.007
is confident

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:35.074
that they have a handle on this.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.843
Now, Ali, the question is,

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.111
what does that mean in New York,

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:40.013
in Chicago, in L.A.,

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.748
where there are they prepared?

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.383
Well, they've been preparing.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:44.250
And, you know,

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.451
I think they are waiting

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.053
and watching carefully

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:48.087
and I think they're all going to be

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.756
watching this tape.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:50.623
John, thank you.

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:51.991
Shimon, thank you very much

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:52.959
for being on the ground for us.

